<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Gonzaga-Nevers</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonzaga-Nevers was a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga family</a> descended from Louis Gonzaga, who became Duke of Nevers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> by marriage in 1565. When the main line died out in 1627, his son Charles I Gonzaga-Nevers inherited Mantua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-mantuan-succession">War of the Mantuan Succession</a>. The branch ruled Mantua until Ferdinando Carlo was deposed by the emperor in 1708.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga-nevers.jpg" alt="House of Gonzaga-Nevers" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Gianfrancesco_I_Gonzaga,_Marquess_of_Mantua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
